  "full-article-text": "<p id=\"\">How long is an epoch on Radix?</p><p id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-an-epoch-2\"><strong id=\"\">Epochs</strong></a> as part of the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-the-radix-roadmap\"><strong id=\"\">Olympia</strong></a> release on the <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-are-the-radix-public-network-and-radix-ledger\"><strong id=\"\">Radix Public Network</strong></a><strong id=\"\"> </strong>should generally be under 2 hours long.&nbsp;</p><p id=\"\">The precise length of an epoch is based on the rate that the network produces <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-the-difference-between-a-full-node-validator-node-and-archive-node\"><strong id=\"\">“versions”</strong></a> (similar to blocks on <a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/what-is-a-blockchain\"><strong id=\"\">blockchain</strong></a> networks) rather than a fixed “wall clock” time.</p><p id=\"\"><strong id=\"\">Further reading:</strong></p><ul id=\"\"><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-an-epoch-2\"><strong id=\"\">What’s an epoch?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-do-xrd-emissions-work\"><strong id=\"\">How do XRD emissions work?</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/how-xrd-staking-emissions-rewards-are-calculated-for-token-holders\"><strong id=\"\">How XRD staking emissions rewards are calculated - general</strong></a></li><li id=\"\"><a id=\"\" href=\"https://learn.radixdlt.com/article/whats-the-difference-between-a-full-node-validator-node-and-archive-node\"><strong id=\"\">What are “versions” and what does “versions per second” mean?</strong></a></li></ul>",
